@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-calendar`

-- ca-tests-red.l4
--
-- TEN DELIBERATELY FAILING EXPECTATIONS.  Every `#ASSERT` below states a plausible reading that the text of the Act rules out.
-- Each is expected to FAIL, and check.sh is told to expect exactly ten failures from this file (`expected_failed`), so that a failure
-- here is a pass of the encoding and an eleventh failure, or a fewer, is a finding.
-- None of these is a test of the encoding against its own output: each states a reading the statute rejects, and the section that rejects it is named.

-- RED 1.  "A month after 31 January ends on 3 March" (the overflow reading: 31 January plus one month is 31 February, which rolls over).
-- Section 28(c): "if that month has no day with that number, the last day of that month".  The answer is 28 February.
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 1 `months after` (YMD 2025 1 31))'s `the last day`) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 3

-- RED 2.  "Thirty days from 1 January ends on 30 January" (the start day counted as day one).
-- Section 27(4): a time expressed to be "from" a specified day does not include that day.  The answer is 31 January.
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 30 `days from` (YMD 2026 1 1))'s `the last day`) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30

-- RED 3.  "Saturday is a holiday, so a time that ends on Saturday 7 March 2026 moves to Monday 9 March."
-- Section 35(1) "holiday" lists Sunday and does not list Saturday.  The answer is Saturday 7 March.
#ASSERT `the last day for a thing under the Act's own dated holidays when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 7) `given the other holidays` `no other holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9

-- RED 4.  "An Act assented to on 10 March 2026 that says nothing about commencement comes into force from the expiration of 10 March (that is, from 11 March)."
-- Section 6(2)(a): "on the expiration of the day immediately before the day the Act was assented to": the expiration of 9 March.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of the provision of an Act` (`Commencement facts of an Act` WITH `the day the Act was assented to` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `what the provision says about when it comes into force` IS `it names no day`) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 10))

-- RED 5.  "A regulation of an exempted class, made on 10 March 2026 and silent, comes into force from the expiration of 10 March."
-- Section 6(2)(b): "the expiration of the day immediately before the day the regulation was made": the expiration of 9 March.
#ASSERT `the coming into force of a regulation` (`Commencement facts of a regulation` WITH `the day the regulation was made` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `what the regulation says about when it comes into force` IS `it names no day`, `the day it was registered under section 6 of the Statutory Instruments Act, if it has been` IS NOTHING, `it is of a class exempted from the application of subsection 5(1) of that Act` IS TRUE) EQUALS `in force from` (`the expiration of` (YMD 2026 3 10))

-- RED 6.  "Two years after 28 February 2024 ends on 27 February 2026" (the anniversary minus one day).
-- Sections 37(1) and 28: twenty-four months; the day with the same number in the last month counted, 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 2 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 28))'s `the last day`) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 27

-- RED 7.  "A person born on 15 March 2000 attains 18 on 14 March 2018" (the day before the birthday).
-- Section 30: not attained "until the commencement of the anniversary": 15 March 2018.
#ASSERT `a person born on` (YMD 2000 3 15) `has attained` 18 `years of age on` (YMD 2018 3 14)

-- RED 8.  "One year after 29 February 2024 ends on 1 March 2025" (rolling forward past a missing 29 February).
-- Section 28(c): the last day of that month, 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT ((`the period of` 1 `years after` (YMD 2024 2 29))'s `the last day`) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1

-- RED 9.  "Between events on 1 March and 10 March there are nine clear days."
-- Section 27(1): the days on which the events happen are both excluded: 2 to 9 March is eight.
#ASSERT `the number of clear days between` (YMD 2026 3 1) `and` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS 9

-- RED 10.  "A time that ends on Sunday 8 March 2026, with Monday 9 March also a holiday, may be met on Monday 9 March" (only one holiday skipped).
-- Section 26: "the day next following that is not a holiday": Tuesday 10 March.
#ASSERT `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` (YMD 2026 3 8) `given the holidays` (GIVEN d YIELD `is a Sunday` d OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
